// std/nat.dag -- Natural numbers (ℕ) as semiring over the abstract counting carrier.
//
// Layer 2 of the construction chain authored in
// `docs/design-numeric-construction.md`:
//
//   Magnitude → Nat → Int → Rational → Real
//
// `Nat = Semiring<Magnitude>` says "ℕ is the algebra of addition + multiplication
// (with identities 0 and 1) over the unbounded counting carrier `Magnitude`."
// No additive inverse — `Semiring` is the right algebra layer for ℕ; `Int`
// extends to `AbelianGroup<Nat>` in a later slice (Grothendieck construction).
//
// TRACKED SCAFFOLD (algebra-strength sharpening) — P5 dissolution trigger:
//   The denotational note at `dsl/std/algebra.dag:54` says
//     "Nat inhabits CommutativeSemiring  (because (Nat, *, 1) is a commutative monoid)"
//   but `dsl/std/algebra.dag` declares only `type Semiring<T>` (no
//   `type CommutativeSemiring<T>`). `Semiring<Magnitude>` is the closest
//   honest algebra surface available today; multiplicative commutativity
//   of ℕ is true denotationally but not yet pinned structurally in the
//   substrate. Precedent for the sharpening is already in algebra.dag:
//   `Monoid → CommutativeMonoid` is the same shape (`algebra.dag:111-122`).
//
//   **Dissolution trigger:** when an algebra-strength sharpening slice
//   introduces `type CommutativeSemiring<T>` to `dsl/std/algebra.dag`,
//   change this declaration to
//     `type Nat = CommutativeSemiring<Magnitude>`
//   and update the structural ratchet
//   `nat_resolves_to_semiring_over_magnitude` in
//   `src/v3/compiler/tests/integration/m2_substrate_inhabitance_test.rs`
//   to match the new template id. No consumer migration needed —
//   `CommutativeSemiring<T>` extends `Semiring<T>` at the algebra layer;
//   downstream callers see no signature change.
//
//   The construction-chain progression in `docs/design-numeric-construction.md`
//   sequences concept-layer introduction first (this slice + Slices 3+);
//   algebra-strength sharpening is a parallel lane (see PR #1399 inbox
//   discussion at #1130).
//
// CONSUMERS: none in this slice. Refinements `Nat<N>` (later slices, gated
// on T-V2-Retirement per design doc §"path (a) coordination") parameterize
// the namespace to bind concrete bit-width at grounding time.
//
// HARD BOUNDARIES:
//   - Carrier is `Magnitude`, the canonical algebraic counting carrier.
//     `Word64` / `Word128` (and `Byte`/`Word16`/`Word32`) at `dsl/std/bit.dag`
//     remain **storage refinements** at the bit-/byte-record layer; they are
//     not alternate `Nat`/`Magnitude` authorities.
//   - No tokenizer / `LitInt` / literal-grammar changes.
//   - No refinement syntax (`Nat<N>`, `where bits <= N`) — gated on
//     T-V2-Retirement per design doc.
//   - No migration of legacy `dsl/std/integer.dag` `Semiring<Word*>` / `OrderedRing<Word*>`
//     chain — sequenced for design doc §6 cascade slice.

module std.nat

import std.algebra { Semiring }
import std.magnitude { Magnitude }

type Nat = Semiring<Magnitude>
